From: openEuler RISC-V Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] libheal: link the engine support sources

libheal includes imageSynth.c in addition to the core engine, but its Meson
source list omits the map, coordinate, target-pixel, ordering, bounds, and
statistics implementations used by those translation units. Add the same
support sources already used by libresynthesizer so the upstream testHealLib
functional harness links against complete implementations.
---
 lib/meson.build | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/lib/meson.build b/lib/meson.build
index ea2634d..6882f22 100644
--- a/lib/meson.build
+++ b/lib/meson.build
@@ -19,6 +19,12 @@ libheal_sources = [
   'engine.c',
   'engineParams.c',
   'imageFormat.c',
   'progress.c',
+  'stats.c',
+  'targetPixels.c',
+  'map.c',
+  'targetPointsOrder.c',
+  'coordinates.c',
+  'bounds.c',
 ]
 
 # libresynthesizer is much more general,
-- 
2.51.0
